{"id":12148,"date":"2023-11-29T19:25:43","date_gmt":"2023-11-30T03:25:43","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/coding-on-the-web-2\/"},"modified":"2024-10-29T15:05:51","modified_gmt":"2024-10-29T22:05:51","slug":"getting-started-python-for-robolink","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/getting-started-python-for-robolink\/","title":{"rendered":"0.2 Getting Started with Python for Robolink"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ea1f\" name=\"6a22138d7ea1f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Before You Fly<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1730227373096{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>PRE-FLIGHT WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise caution while piloting your drone. To prolong the longevity of your drone, avoid flying into walls or other objects. Prior to takeoff, please review lesson <em>0.2 \u201cBefore You Fly\u201d.<\/em><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7eb9d\" name=\"6a22138d7eb9d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Accessing Python for Robolink<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_single_image image=&#8221;11930&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<em>Note: As this is a brand-new product for Robolink, we are continually making improvements to provide the most seamless experience possible. However, if you run into any issues with the platform, please have your teacher, parent, or coach <a href=\"https:\/\/www.robolink.com\/pages\/contact-us\">reach out to us<\/a> immediately so that we can begin looking into a solution.<\/em><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>To start programming on the web, go to: <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/python\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Python for Robolink.<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Once there, follow the steps below to learn more about the features of <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>\u00a0and how to get started programming from a web browser.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ec68\" name=\"6a22138d7ec68\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Update Google Chrome<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<em>Note: You must use the Google Chrome web browser to access Python for Robolink.<\/em>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12074&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]If you do not all ready have Chrome installed, please go here: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.google.com\/chrome\/\">Install Google Chrome Now<\/a><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Additionally, it is important that your Google Chrome is on the latest version.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To check which version of Chrome you have:<\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Click the three dots in the top right corner of Chrome<\/span><\/li>\n<li>Click on \u201cHelp\u201d near the bottom of the menu<\/li>\n<li>Click on \u201cAbout Google Chrome\u201d<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12087&#8243; img_size=&#8221;Full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]You may find that Google Chrome is already up-to-date or that it starts updating automatically. If it is not up-to-date, go ahead and update now.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ecf8\" name=\"6a22138d7ecf8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect the Controller<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In order to program your CoDrone EDU from any platform, you will need to connect your controller to your device using the cable that came with your CoDrone EDU. <strong>It is important that you use the cable because it is designed to transfer data. Not all USB cables are capable of transferring data.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7150&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Once plugged in, if your drone does not switch to <strong>LINK<\/strong> state, you may have the wrong cable or the cable may be broken.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8764&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ed90\" name=\"6a22138d7ed90\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Power on the Drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, power on the drone using a charged battery.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;4616&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your drone should pair to the controller, as indicated by the solid LED on the drone and controller. If your drone and controller are not paired, watch <a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/X-gyVk0YlzE\">the below video.<\/a> <\/span><\/p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Pairing CoDrone EDU to Controller\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/X-gyVk0YlzE?feature=oembed&#038;enablejsapi=1&#038;origin=https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ee49\" name=\"6a22138d7ee49\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connecting to Python for Robolink<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Once your controller is plugged in,<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the green \u201cConnect\u201d button on the bottom left of the screen<\/li>\n<li>Select your controller in the pop-up window<\/li>\n<li>Click the blue \u201cConnect\u201d button<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>If you do not see your controller in the window, check that your controller is in <strong>LINK<\/strong> state or use a different cable.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11968&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Once your controller and drone are connected to <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>, you will be able to see the drone information window in the bottom-left corner.<\/p>\n<p>Here, you can change the speed, set the trim values, and see your battery percentage.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11971&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7ef4f\" name=\"6a22138d7ef4f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Running Code in Python for Robolink<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In the middle of the page, you will see a space for you to write your own code. The section is labeled as <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\"># Welcome to Python for Robolink! Write your Python code below.<\/code>.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Upon creating a new Python file, starter code will be generated for you that imports the CoDrone EDU library, creates a new drone object, pairs the drone, and closes the drone connection at the completion of your program.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE NOTE:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol class=\"ProsemirrorEditor-list\" data-pm-slice=\"3 3 []\">\n<li class=\"ProsemirrorEditor-listItem\" data-list-indent=\"1\" data-list-type=\"bulleted\"><em>Python for Robolink<\/em> currently does not support custom object names for the drone. At all times, use the following line of code to establish the drone: <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">drone = Drone()<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li class=\"ProsemirrorEditor-listItem\" data-list-indent=\"1\" data-list-type=\"bulleted\">\u00a0In the case you accidentally erase any of the starter code statements, opening a new tab in <em>Python for Robolink<\/em> will cause them to reappear.<\/li>\n<li class=\"ProsemirrorEditor-listItem\" data-list-indent=\"1\" data-list-type=\"bulleted\">If there is a typo in your statements, <em>Python for Robolink<\/em> will notify you in the console.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To get familiar with <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>, print \u201cHello, world\u201d by typing it in the middle section of the code editor. You can also copy and paste this code:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">print(\"Hello, world\")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13022&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1724794705790{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"84\" height=\"85\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">The stop command should only be used in emergencies or when safety has become a concern. In all other circumstances, you should use the land command to bring your drone safely to the ground.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To run or stop code, use the \u201cRun Code\u201d, \u201cStop\u201d, or \u201cLand\u201d buttons at the top of the page. When flying, the \u201cStop\u201d button will emergency stop the motors, so we recommend using the \u201cLand\u201d button whenever possible if you need to interrupt your code. Even if your drone is not flying, you can use these buttons to interrupt your program.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13028&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7efe9\" name=\"6a22138d7efe9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Console Window<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When you run the code, any outputs or errors will appear in the console at the bottom of the screen.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13027&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Python console is also helpful for debugging, or finding errors in your code. You can use the <code>print()<\/code> function to print out values and test whether your programs are running correctly.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7f0b4\" name=\"6a22138d7f0b4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Managing Your Python Files<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]When you click \u201cRun\u201d, <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>\u00a0will run the code on the current tab. If you want to test out a new idea without closing your first program, click the \u201c+\u201d to create a new file. We recommend renaming each file to keep your programs organized. You can do so by double-clicking on the current title in the tab of the Python file.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13023&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<em><strong>Be sure to save your programs before closing the tabs.<\/strong> <\/em>To save your programs, you will need to download the Python files. Unlike other applications, your programs will not save automatically. If you were to close your web browser, you would lose all the work you did.<\/p>\n<p>To save your files:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the \u201cMenu\u201d<\/li>\n<li>You then have the option to download one or all of the files to your device<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13024&#8243; img_size=&#8221;Full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]When you decide to come back to a program, you will need to open in <em>Python for Robolink.<\/em><\/p>\n<p>To open your files:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the \u201cMenu\u201d<\/li>\n<li>Select \u201cOpen Python files\u2026\u201d<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Your Python file should then open up where you left off![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13025&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22138d7f15c\" name=\"6a22138d7f15c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Review<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned the basics of <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>! Let&#8217;s review:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>In <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>, you must connect your controller to run drone-related code.<\/li>\n<li>When writing code involving the CoDrone, you must include the statements provided in the <em>Python for Robolink<\/em> starter code.<\/li>\n<li>Don&#8217;t forget to download your Python file to save your work. We recommend organizing your files in a particular folder or uploading them to a safe place online like a school account.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The next lesson goes over how to install and setup PyCharm for macOS or Windows machines. If you will only be using <em>Python for Robolink<\/em>, skip ahead to <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/quiz\/1-1-first-flight-2\/\">1.1: First Flight.<\/a>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8699&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Before You Fly [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1730227373096{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] PRE-FLIGHT WARNING Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise caution while piloting your drone. To prolong&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/getting-started-python-for-robolink\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4733,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3875,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[13994,4328,14401,13996,13998,2134,14000],"class_list":["post-12148","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-browser-en","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-chrome-en","lesson-tag-chromebook-en","lesson-tag-python","lesson-tag-web-en","module-918-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/12148","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":19,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/12148\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13100,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/12148\/revisions\/13100"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4733"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=12148"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=12148"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=12148"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}